<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    GrammarBar.app — plan v2 §6.

    App Sandbox ON, network client OFF, user-selected read-only ON.

    `com.apple.security.network.client` is deliberately ABSENT rather than set to
    <false/>: this is the process that handles user text, and plan v2 §7's privacy
    statement is "the app's only network use is an optional model download, done by
    a separate helper". Adding the key here — even as false — invites someone to
    flip it to true later, and NFR1 says the main app makes zero connections.

    NOT VERIFIED: no .xcodeproj exists yet, so nothing has loaded this file. It has
    not been checked against `codesign --display --entitlements`, and the sandbox
    behaviour it implies is unverified until the XcodeGen project (project.yml,
    another workstream) builds a real app target.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
